e,"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm approving PKT-0071. It answers the question the packet asked, and I found nothing that needs fixing.\n\n**Goal:** The packet asked for before and after numbers for PKT-0066. `baseline.md` now has them: a table with self times for the font-collection functions, broken down by case and variant, plus the per-run numbers and how to reproduce the measurement. The main finding is that the incremental path is never taken during remote typing, because every typing batch also carries a `CTableId` change. That finding comes from instrumenting user B, which is direct evidence, not a guess from timings.\n\n**Contract:** No sdkjs code changed; the sdkjs diff is empty. This repository's diff touches four files: `baseline.md` (the only file in the target), the packet file, `friction.jsonl` and the spawn request. All are within the budget of 6 files and 800 lines.\n\n**Executor log, follow-up and friction:** The log is filled in, including the commit hash that no longer exists, the choice to build both versions the same way, and why the existing profiling scripts weren't used. The follow-up is listed under Spawned packets and exists in `.theseus/spawn/`. Its contract keeps the full walk as the fallback for any unknown change type, and it carries over the expected gain of about 140 ms per 30 changes. The friction line was added.\n\n**Things the tests don't catch:**\n- The report calls the after/before gap \"noise\", which is a slightly strong word. In the typing case all three \"after\" runs (212 / 146 / 226 ms) are at or above every \"before\" run (133–144 ms). That is still consistent with noise, since the full walk is the same code in both builds and the new functions take 0.1 ms. But with 3 runs per side and no spread reported, the data can't show that the difference is zero. When the follow-up re-measures, it should use more runs or interleave the two variants.\n- The style-edit fallback case was measured with a change to the default paragraph style. That is a reasonable stand-in for \"a style edit\", and the packet asked for one.\n- The harness lives in the scratchpad, not in the repository, because the target allowed no new files. The method is written down well enough to rerun it.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE measurement recorded in baseline.md with root cause (CTableId fallback) and follow-up spawned; contract respected","ttft_ms":2040,"type":"result","duration_ms":16670,"uuid":"78816907-8607-42fb-ad9b-aeb4a624fb0f","ttft_stream_ms":799,"time_to_request_ms":326,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":184,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":5,"input_attachments":33,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":15,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":6,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":29,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":41,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":159,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":213,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":227,"process_anon_mib_result":139,"process_peak_rss_mib":253,"process_cpu_ms_turn":849,"process_wall_ms_turn":16669,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":380,"process_wall_ms_streaming":14180,"main_stream_count":4,"main_stream_event_count":257,"main_stream_chunk_count":74,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":20,"cpu_ms":30,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":8,"ambient_wait_ms":20,"render_ms":2,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_frame_ms":800,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":5423093,"warm_spare_claimed":false,"flag_fetch_kick":"started_in_init_warm","time_origin_ms":1793664118557.721